    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.shape — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.shape#\n\n- \n*property* DataFrame.shape[source]#\n- Return a tuple representing the dimensionality of the DataFrame. See also \n  - `ndarray.shape`\n  - Tuple of array dimensions.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({'col1': [1, 2], 'col2': [3, 4]}) >>> df.shape (2, 2) >>> df = pd.DataFrame({'col1': [1, 2], 'col2': [3, 4], ... 'col3': [5, 6]}) >>> df.shape (2, 3)",
